# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: through a header writing `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored
# "-Wincompatible-pointer-types"`, `take_a(p: B)` against `int take_a(struct
# a *)`, a handle of another tag (defect 029's class), built and printed `1`.
#
# CAUSE: the build's `-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types` is the check, and
# the header's pragma outranked it at the probe.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-a-handle-of-another-tag-is-refused-through-the-pragma.h"
    record A tag a
    record B tag b
    function take_a(p: B) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(take_a(nullptr))
